==English==

===Etymology===
{{compound|en|chair|person}}, after {{m|en|chairman}} and {{m|en|chairwoman}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-chairperson.wav|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|chairpeople}}

# A [[chairman]] or [[chairwoman]], someone who [[preside]]s over a [[meeting]], [[board]], etc.
#: {{ux|en|She was the '''chairperson''' of the board and she [[preside]]d over the meeting.}}

====Usage notes====
In modern usage, terms like {{m|en|chair}}, {{m|en|moderator}}, {{m|en|coordinator}}, {{m|en|presiding}} {{m|en|officer}}, {{m|en|group}} {{m|en|leader}}, {{m|en|head}}, {{m|en|facilitator}}, and so forth, are often more common. However, ''chairperson'' is usually found in African and Asian English varieties, like in India, the Philippines, and South Africa.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|chair}}
* {{l|en|presiding}} [[officer]], [[presider]]

====Derived terms====
* [[vice chairperson]]

